A||||3||acehilton||Shimmy and Bangs||||1||
Z||000000||acehilton||05-18-2001||11:19 PM||||Howdy all,<P>My 86 coupe has developed an interesting problem.  At speed (aprox. 60 - 70 mph) the car has developed a shake.  It is coming though the steering wheel.  The wheel has had some slop (about 1/2" side to side) in it since I bought the car a little over a year ago.  Below highway speeds the shake is gone.  During slow speed turning, parking lots, intersections, ect..., the is a loud bang that comes from the front of the car. I thought that I had a wheel out of balance, but the bang at slow speed, stop to stop turns has me wondering.  <P>Just for general information, the car is stock, no modifications at all. <P>I am thinking that the rack and pinion needs to be rebuilt/replaced, but I wanted to see if anyone has any other ideas (ball joints, tie rod ends, suspension bushings, ect..), and what tests or inspections I can do to narrow down the problem.<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||05-18-2001||11:46 PM||||Sounds like you know what all to check, just a matter of getting under there.  Shaking is usually inner tie rod end. or shifted belt in tire, but u say u have play in wheel-follow that up.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||05-19-2001||08:17 PM||||You might want to check out the wheel bearings while you're at it. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bob Englert||05-19-2001||09:01 PM||||Personally I would suggest doing a complete rebuild of the front suspension (control arm bushings, ball joints, tie rod ends, and possibly a rebuilt rack).  The parts are not all that expensive and it is A LOT easier to do it all at once while things are apart than it is to replace a parts and keep chasing the problem.  <P>I have rebuilt FR suspensions on 4 Fieros, the before and after difference is dramatic.  The car feels so much tighter after it is done and you get a good alignment.  Doing my maroon 87 GT right now, slow going since it was Michigan car and things are pretty rusty.  <P>Worth the effort IMO.  <P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
